well it's interesting that the palace  have said they are appointing a  diversity  chief just weeks after the fallout over  the oprah  interview which of course saw the royal  family engulfed  in a very serious and unprecedented race  round now we learn that they are  in the process of hiring a chief of  staff my understanding is that this was  an appointment that was always going to  happen  it was something the royal family  thought was important as it  modernized and progress but it certainly  seems to have been  speed tracked post oprah and really  given paramount  importance now so we've seen that the  institution now  are reacting to that interview that  diversity is now very much  at the forefront of the palace and i  think the simple fact is that these  allegations of racism have stung they  have  hurt the royal family publicly and  privately  um as far as the royals are concerned  prince charles who has done so much to  promote  diversity and particularly in the uk and  around the commonwealth  and for prince william who is you know  championing an  anti-racism movement here in the uk  in sports particularly in football you  know these claims have  frankly been devastating and as far as  the royal family is concerned these  allegations are deeply damaging they are  very  upsetting i think we saw that very much  with prince william responding  when asked if the royal family was  racist and he said this is  very much not a racist family i think  you're now going to see even more  evidence of them really  proving just that i'm sure that megan  and harry would very much want to be  involved with discussions about how the  palace might become a more diverse  workplace but the feeling i get is this  is very much handled  in-house this is being taken care of by  courtiers with the oversight of the  queen and members of the royal family  but  essentially this is an in palace  operation and i think it's quite telling  that megan and harry haven't been  invited to be part of the investigation  into the bullying claims  against megan they're being kept quite  deliberately distant from that  and i would expect that it will be very  much the same with this  whole movement towards a more diverse  working operation at buckingham palace  the couple have cut their ties with the  palace  with the courtiers there's really no  reason for them to be a part of these  discussions but i think the point is  the palace have heard what the couple  have to say they have listened  and now measures being put in place to  act on some of those challenges
 

